{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user submitted a complex stitch task (Task ID: 5308) to implement specific requirements from srd031-sha1sum in the go-unix-utils project. The task requires implementing:\n   - R3.2: `--tag` produces BSD tag format regardless of -b/-t flags\n   - R4.1: Must exit 0 when all files are processed and all verified digests match\n   - R4.2: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, any digest fails, or checksum file is unreadable\n   - R4.3: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n   \n   The task description says: \"Complete R3.2 check mode and add R4.1-R4.3 functionality\" and specifies modifying `cmd/sha1sum/main.go` and `cmd/sha1sum/sha1sum_test.go`. The acceptance criteria require compilation, passing tests, and feature-completeness of all 12 SRD requirements (R1.1 through R4.3).\n\n   CRITICAL CONSTRAINT: Git is managed externally by the orchestrator. Do NOT run any git commands. Do NOT modify files outside the specified list. Do NOT explore the filesystem.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - SHA-1 digest computation using Go's `crypto/sha1`\n   - GNU checksum format: `HASH  FILENAME` (text) or `HASH *FILENAME` (binary)\n   - BSD tag format: `SHA1 (FILENAME) = HASH`\n   - Differential testing against `gsha1sum` reference binary from Homebrew\n   - `pkg/hashutil` shared library: `VerifyChecksums`, `DigestFiles`, `CheckOptions`, `HashConfig`\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` for differential testing harness\n   - Exit code conventions: 0 for success, 1 for any failure\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd031-sha1sum.yaml`** (read, not modified)\n     - Source